  "hypothesis": "The calibrated-probability BLOCK rule (Platt map + calibration gate, ECE <= 0.05) is the wrong instrument for M4, which asks for precision on what is flagged. Selective blocking -- a per-family raw-score threshold chosen on training folds only as the lowest one whose Wilson 95% lower bound on flagged precision is >= 0.95 -- reaches the M4 precision bar on held-out repositories where the calibrated rule offers no BLOCK.\n",
